```
Reason:
The restriction that required the `NETIF_F_HW_CSUM` feature to be enabled for the `NETIF_F_HW_TLS_TX` feature to be active inadvertently blocked devices that only supported IP checksum (`NETIF_F_IP_CSUM`) and IPv6 checksum (`NETIF_F_IPV6_CSUM`), preventing them from utilizing TLS TX offload functionality.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
bool ip_csum = (features & (NETIF_F_IP_CSUM | NETIF_F_IPV6_CSUM)) ==
    (NETIF_F_IP_CSUM | NETIF_F_IPV6_CSUM);
bool hw_csum = features & NETIF_F_HW_CSUM;

if (!ip_csum && !hw_csum) {
    netdev_dbg(dev, "Dropping TLS TX HW offload feature since no CSUM feature.\n");
    features &= ~NETIF_F_HW_TLS_TX;
}
```
Reason:
The fix introduces a check that allows the `NETIF_F_HW_TLS_TX` feature to remain active if either `NETIF_F_IP_CSUM` or `NETIF_F_IPV6_CSUM` is enabled, thus accommodating devices that support these checksum features without requiring `NETIF_F_HW_CSUM`.

